nat44-ei: let ip4-local find the hairpinning node

With an inside interface, a packet from inside to the outside address and a
mapped port is translated by in2out (source to the outside address), looked
up, and lands on ip4-local, where nat44-ei-hairpinning should rewrite the
destination to the inside service. EI enables that node on the ip4-local
arc of local0, and ip4-local starts the arc on ip.rx_sw_if_index. But
ip4-local sets that field only in its source check, which it skips for
packets marked VNET_BUFFER_F_IS_NATED (IP_LOCAL_PACKET_TYPE_NAT), so for
exactly these packets the field kept whatever the reassembly data that
shares it left there, the arc ran on no real interface and the packet was
punted ("ip4-local: unknown ip protocol"). Hairpinning never worked; VPP
master has the same code.

Set ip.rx_sw_if_index to local0 where in2out marks a packet NATed. Nothing
after in2out reads the reassembly fields it overlaps. Only the NAT plugin
changes.

With the output feature alone (no inside interface), packets to the outside
address never pass in2out and are not hairpinned; that is unchanged.

Verified in an isolated VPP: from an inside host to the outside address and
a static mapping that leads back to it, TCP connects and UDP gets its answer
from the mapped port, with in/out interfaces and with the output feature plus
an inside interface; without this patch the SYN is punted. Test:
tests/integration/integration_nat44_partial_checksum.py --nat ei.

--- a/src/plugins/nat/nat44-ei/nat44_ei_in2out.c
+++ b/src/plugins/nat/nat44-ei/nat44_ei_in2out.c
@@ -1577,6 +1577,10 @@
 				nat_value_get_session_index (&value0));
 
       b0->flags |= VNET_BUFFER_F_IS_NATED;
+      /* ip4-local skips its source check for NATed packets and so never
+       * sets rx_sw_if_index, which picks the ip4-local features; set it to
+       * local0, where nat44-ei-hairpinning is enabled */
+      vnet_buffer (b0)->ip.rx_sw_if_index = 0;
 
       old_addr0 = ip0->src_address.as_u32;
       ip0->src_address = s0->out2in.addr;
@@ -1818,6 +1822,10 @@
 				nat_value_get_session_index (&value1));
 
       b1->flags |= VNET_BUFFER_F_IS_NATED;
+      /* ip4-local skips its source check for NATed packets and so never
+       * sets rx_sw_if_index, which picks the ip4-local features; set it to
+       * local0, where nat44-ei-hairpinning is enabled */
+      vnet_buffer (b1)->ip.rx_sw_if_index = 0;
 
       old_addr1 = ip1->src_address.as_u32;
       ip1->src_address = s1->out2in.addr;
@@ -2089,6 +2097,10 @@
 				nat_value_get_session_index (&value0));
 
       b0->flags |= VNET_BUFFER_F_IS_NATED;
+      /* ip4-local skips its source check for NATed packets and so never
+       * sets rx_sw_if_index, which picks the ip4-local features; set it to
+       * local0, where nat44-ei-hairpinning is enabled */
+      vnet_buffer (b0)->ip.rx_sw_if_index = 0;
 
       old_addr0 = ip0->src_address.as_u32;
       ip0->src_address = s0->out2in.addr;
